From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:12:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tests/color-management: Cover mastering metadata and light
 levels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the two regressions that expected set_mastering_display_primaries
and set_mastering_luminance to raise unsupported_feature, now that they
are supported, with:

 - /wayland/creator-params/mastering-luminance-invalid: a mastering
   maximum equal to the minimum (1 cd/m² both) raises
   invalid_luminance on the creator-params interface.
 - /wayland/creator-params/mastering-primaries-twice,
   .../mastering-luminance-twice, .../max-cll-twice and
   .../max-fall-twice: a repeated request raises already_set.
 - /wayland/creator-params/max-fall-above-max-cll: create raises
   invalid_luminance for MaxFALL 401 with MaxCLL 400.
 - /wayland/creator-params/v1-max-cll-above-mastering: on a version 1
   creator, MaxCLL above the mastering maximum raises
   invalid_luminance at create; .../v2-light-levels: the same values
   are accepted on version 2.
 - /wayland/creator-params/extended-target-volume: collinear mastering
   primaries and an unrepresentable coordinate fail with the
   'unsupported' cause and the connection survives; P3-D65 and BT.2020
   mastering primaries in a BT.2020 volume, BT.2020 mastering primaries
   in a BT.709 volume, and reference white above the maximum luminance
   are accepted.
 - /wayland/creator-params/mastering-round-trip: the client finds
   set_mastering_display_primaries and extended_target_volume
   advertised. HDR10 metadata (P3-D65, 0.0001 to 1000 cd/m², MaxCLL 800,
   MaxFALL 300) is retained exactly on the surface's color state, gives
   an effective peak of 800 cd/m² (from
   clutter_color_state_params_get_peak_headroom(), against 10000 for
   plain PQ), makes a state unequal to the same encoding without
   metadata yet needing no conversion to or from it; MaxCLL and MaxFALL
   of 0 declare nothing (equal state, equal hash); MaxFALL alone is kept
   and does not lower the effective peak.

Protocol error cases expect the disconnect warning, as the existing
ones do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
